[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68857,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal papillary adenomas are unencapsulated tumours with papillary, tubular, or tubulopapillary configurations of low histological grade and a diameter of &le;&nbsp;15&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68858,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8260/0 Papillary adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68859,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F35 &amp; XH09B0 Benign neoplasm of urinary organs &amp; Papillary adenoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68860,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> tubulopapillary adenoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> renal adenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68861,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68862,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary adenomas usually occur in the renal cortex, particularly in the capsular or subcapsular area.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68863,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Virtually all papillary adenomas are clinically silent and discovered as incidental findings.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68864,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detailed sectioning of autopsy kidneys has detected papillary adenomas in 10% of individuals aged 21&ndash;40&nbsp;years and in 40% of those aged 70&ndash;90&nbsp;years {9503505}. They are more frequent in elderly patients, patients on long-term haemodialysis, and patients with renal vascular disease or glomerulosclerosis {30418186}. They have been reported in 33% of patients with acquired cystic disease and in 14% of patients undergoing transplantation for end-stage renal disease {12028461}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68865,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "<p>Papillary adenomas have been reported in kidneys bearing renal cell carcinoma {1942266}, and they are common in the kidneys of patients with hereditary papillary renal carcinoma {10647647}. This lesion may occasionally be found entrapped in oncocytic tumours {31444626}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-28T15:47:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68866,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Whole-exome sequencing has demonstrated that <em>KMT2C</em> mutations may be an important early event in the evolution of papillary adenoma {31381885}. Papillary adenomas frequently show trisomy&nbsp;7 and 17 in addition to loss of the Y&nbsp;chromosome {14559990; 10398084}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68867,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary adenomas arise in the renal cortex and are often subcapsular; larger adenomas are often wedged-shaped, with the base at the cortical surface. In cases of numerous papillary adenomas, the term &ldquo;renal adenomatosis&rdquo; is applied.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68868,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary adenomas show papillary, tubular, or tubulopapillary architecture. Adenoma cells have predominantly pale and scant cytoplasm, round to oval nuclei with stippled to clumped chromatin, minimal nuclear pleomorphism, inconspicuous nucleoli, and absent or very rare mitosis. Foamy macrophages and psammoma bodies may be present. Papillary adenomas are unencapsulated and blend with adjacent benign tubular epithelium {13628880}.</p>\r\n<p>Most adenomas show expression of CK7, CD10, and AMACR {7531836}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68869,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 6,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-09T17:52:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68870,
